\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Placeholder: Simplified schematic of the proposed adaptive Surrogate Transition framework. The uncertainty-aware POD–GP surrogate is used to construct an approximate likelihood for inexpensive first-stage acceptance decisions. During the adaptive phase, posterior-guided acquisition identifies new high-fidelity evaluations to enrich the surrogate, while the Surrogate Transition subchain length is adjusted according to the estimated surrogate error. Once the surrogate satisfies the prescribed accuracy criterion, adaptation is terminated and the surrogate transition sampler proceeds with a fixed surrogate and transition kernel to generate posterior samples.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:MCMC}{{1}{3}{}{}{}}
